  "final_message": "My channel-removal change had been committed as `782551f` (\"gen\"), so the working tree now holds the reverted state as uncommitted changes. That's the state CI needs. I haven't committed it.\n\n**CI failure.** `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` (enum `web|store|marketplace`). That consumer contract check isn't in this repo, so I couldn't see it before making the change. The premise that nothing reads the field was wrong.\n\n**Fix.** I restored `channel` on the order model, in the `OrderPlaced` event, in request parsing and validation, and in the tests and docs. `npm test` passes 39/39. I couldn't run the CI ARCH-4 check itself, so that part is unconfirmed. The restored event should match what it expects. I didn't re-run `typecheck` or `arch` after the restore.\n\n**Next steps:**\n- Commit the working tree, or revert `782551f` if you prefer a revert commit. I held off because you didn't ask for a commit.\n- If you still want `channel` gone, `analytics-ingest` has to stop requiring it first. After that the removal can be redone, probably with a `schemaVersion` bump.",
